at: Cory Mills (R) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Florida's 7th District is an open seat this cycle after Republican incumbent Cory Mills lost his renomination to Ryan Elijah, who now faces Democrat Bale Dalton. The district leans Republican by about five points, and most expert raters call the race Lean or Likely Republican, though a few see it as a tossup or even a Democratic flip. Prediction markets similarly give the Democrat roughly a one-in-three chance.\n\nDalton has a significant financial edge, raising over four times Elijah's total and benefiting from outside support, while Elijah has run an affordability-focused campaign and avoided debates. With no reliable general-election polling, the race rests on fundamentals, which point to a modest Republican advantage with meaningful uncertainty.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.4211, "margin": -1.21}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.4651, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.3497, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.3248, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.2949, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.3493, "margin": -2.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.3328, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.3464, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.3386, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.3794, "margin": -2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.3754, "margin": -2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.3743, "margin": -2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.4206, "margin": -1.8}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.3495, "margin": -2.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.3089, "margin": -2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.2915, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.3164, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.3185, "margin": -2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.3207, "margin": -2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-11", "p_dem": 0.3242, "margin": -2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-12", "p_d